<refentry version="5.1"
  xml:id="Api.SilikoNodeAssignFromValue"
  xmlns="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook">
<refmeta>
  <refentrytitle>SilikoNodeAssignFromValue</refentrytitle>
</refmeta>

<refnamediv>
  <refname><function>SilikoNodeAssignFromValue</function></refname>
  <refpurpose>Set a node to a value</refpurpose>
</refnamediv>

<refsynopsisdiv>
<programlisting language="C">#include &lt;SilikoCore/Node.h&gt;</programlisting>
<programlisting language="C">void SilikoNodeAssignFromValue(
    SilikoNode *object,
    const SilikoValue *right_side);</programlisting>
</refsynopsisdiv>

<refsection>
<title>Description</title>
<para>The <function>SilikoNodeAssignFromValue</function> function
assigns the value of <varname>right_side</varname> to the object that
<varname>object</varname> points to. If <varname>object</varname>
previously had child nodes, they are passed to
<function>SilikoNodeDestroy</function>. The value from
<varname>right_side</varname> is copied, so the calling context retains
ownership of <varname>right_side</varname>.</para>
</refsection>
</refentry>
